>I recently had the following experience while playing Nethack 2.3.
>After I had received the Hand of Elbereth, a formerly friendly shopkeeper
>refused to let me back into his store.  I had not officially ripped off
>the store, although my dog had been quite actively removing things for
>me.  Does anybody know if the shopkeeper's behavior was related to
>the Hand of Elbereth or whether he was just fed up with having all of
>his stuff disappear whenever I was in the room? 

This is simple.  You are simultaneously invisible and can see
invisible when you are made the Hand of Elbereth.  The shopkeeper
cannot see you, so doesn't move.  Simple.

PS You are also made fire resistant, cold resistant, shock resistant,
and have telepathy.  Not to mention that if you were wielding a long
sword when you were made the HoE it will then have a neat name:
Excalibur.  This is VERY good...

